He was asking how to get to Yeonri-ri.

00:17:30.265 --> 00:17:32.201
Yeonri-ri. Goodness.

00:17:32.201 --> 00:17:33.202
That's great.

00:17:33.202 --> 00:17:34.703
Thank you.

00:17:34.703 --> 00:17:37.106
- Let's go. - Where are they?

00:17:42.378 --> 00:17:43.278
Mr. Seong.

00:17:46.181 --> 00:17:47.950
Hey. That man...

00:17:48.784 --> 00:17:50.552
What is this?

00:17:50.552 --> 00:17:51.420
My goodness.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.123
Mr. Wang. My kids...

00:17:54.123 --> 00:17:55.291
No, don't cry.

00:17:56.025 --> 00:17:57.559
The part-timer said...

00:17:57.559 --> 00:17:59.595
your youngest asked for directions here.

00:17:59.595 --> 00:18:01.030
He couldn't have gone far.

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:03.232
Which way did she say he went? We have to go now.

00:18:03.232 --> 00:18:06.101
You can't drive with your hands trembling like this.

00:18:06.101 --> 00:18:08.270
Seon Ja is the best driver.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:10.239
Where's your car? Let's go together.

00:18:10.239 --> 00:18:11.173
Give us your key.

00:18:11.173 --> 00:18:12.875
Please drive for me. It's this way.

00:18:12.875 --> 00:18:13.876
- Let's go. - Let's go.

00:18:50.579 --> 00:18:51.714
What am I going to do?

00:19:11.266 --> 00:19:13.135
There he is. Over there.

00:19:15.004 --> 00:19:15.971
Wait.

00:19:17.272 --> 00:19:18.207
Wait.

00:19:20.175 --> 00:19:21.043
Wait.

00:19:23.112 --> 00:19:23.946
Hey, wait.

00:19:24.413 --> 00:19:25.914
Stop the truck.

00:19:26.081 --> 00:19:27.216
Stop the truck.

00:19:33.522 --> 00:19:35.891
What? What's he saying?

00:19:35.891 --> 00:19:37.860
Do you not see me?

00:19:40.996 --> 00:19:42.698
There's a kid in the back.

00:19:42.898 --> 00:19:44.266
Mister.

00:19:44.266 --> 00:19:45.934
Please help me.

00:19:45.934 --> 00:19:47.002
No.

00:19:47.002 --> 00:19:48.437
Stay inside.

00:19:49.071 --> 00:19:50.339
It's too dangerous. Stay inside.

00:19:50.873 --> 00:19:53.275
It's dangerous. Stay inside.

00:19:53.475 --> 00:19:54.910
Stop the truck.

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:57.046
There's a kid in the back.

00:19:57.413 --> 00:20:00.316
Stop right there. Stop.

00:20:00.316 --> 00:20:02.318
Why isn't this going any faster?

00:20:02.318 --> 00:20:04.253
I can't lose the truck.

00:20:05.521 --> 00:20:06.422
Come on.

00:20:25.307 --> 00:20:29.011
Am I circling the same place?

00:20:31.146 --> 00:20:34.249
Why does this countryside feel bigger than Canada?

00:20:35.584 --> 00:20:37.119
Where am I?

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:40.723
Am I even headed in the right direction to Yeonri-ri?

00:20:42.891 --> 00:20:44.059
Seong Ji Gu.

00:20:44.893 --> 00:20:47.363
You're smart, so you got home.

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:49.164
Right?

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:00.175
A ghost.

00:21:22.298 --> 00:21:23.532
What are you doing there?

00:21:27.069 --> 00:21:29.471
What's going on here?

00:21:29.872 --> 00:21:32.107
- Are you joking me? - I'm sorry.

00:21:32.107 --> 00:21:33.776
I'll discipline him about this.

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:35.944
Keep a better eye on the kid.

00:21:35.944 --> 00:21:37.813
I will. Thank you for everything.

00:21:39.148 --> 00:21:40.416
Goodbye.

00:21:45.688 --> 00:21:47.289
Are you okay? Are you hurt?

00:21:47.923 --> 00:21:48.857
You must've been really scared.

00:21:49.425 --> 00:21:51.260
Why were you riding in a truck?

00:21:51.994 --> 00:21:54.363
I couldn't find my brother,

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:57.299
and people kept telling me...

00:21:57.299 --> 00:22:00.569
that they would take me to my parents.

00:22:01.337 --> 00:22:02.638
So I was scared.

00:22:03.639 --> 00:22:05.541
You don't know how scary the world can be.

00:22:06.308 --> 00:22:08.110
You could've been in real danger. You know that?

00:22:08.577 --> 00:22:09.979
Running away is serious,

00:22:09.979 --> 00:22:12.047
but getting into a stranger's truck is even worse.

00:22:13.048 --> 00:22:14.450
I'm sorry.

00:22:18.253 --> 00:22:21.323
You should apologize to your parents.

00:22:23.826 --> 00:22:24.693
You've been through a lot.

00:22:25.894 --> 00:22:27.363
Let's go home now.

00:22:42.144 --> 00:22:44.013
Back in our day,

00:22:44.013 --> 00:22:46.181
running away from home was common.

00:22:46.715 --> 00:22:47.616
Right, Seon Ja?

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:50.386
You call that a trend?

00:22:51.086 --> 00:22:52.121
Do they not know how dangerous it can be?

00:22:53.856 --> 00:22:55.391
How can they run away from home?

00:22:58.227 --> 00:22:59.928
I kept thinking on the way here.

00:23:01.430 --> 00:23:02.331
They ran away?

00:23:03.365 --> 00:23:04.199
Why?

00:23:05.367 --> 00:23:07.369
I tried to raise them without depriving them of anything.

00:23:08.971 --> 00:23:11.707
But what parent truly knows what's on their kid's mind?

00:23:13.475 --> 00:23:15.978
I heard you lived apart from them for three years.

00:23:16.712 --> 00:23:19.381
Even when you live with them, you don't know what they're thinking.

00:23:19.715 --> 00:23:21.383
If you lived apart,

00:23:22.952 --> 00:23:24.219
you'd know even less.

00:23:24.219 --> 00:23:27.957
Let's find the kids first and take things slowly...

00:23:27.957 --> 00:23:30.192
Yes, I'm driving slowly right now.

00:23:30.826 --> 00:23:33.462
Seon Ja. A deer! Step on the brake!

00:23:37.099 --> 00:23:38.100
What?

00:23:43.372 --> 00:23:45.307
Ji Sang.

00:23:45.307 --> 00:23:46.675
- What? - What?

00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:49.345
Ji Sang.

00:23:49.345 --> 00:23:50.512
That's not a deer?

00:23:51.814 --> 00:23:52.715
Are you okay?

00:23:53.349 --> 00:23:55.351
- Dad. - What happened to you?

00:23:55.351 --> 00:23:57.453
Everything's fine now.

00:23:57.453 --> 00:23:59.855
I'm here now. Everything's fine.

00:24:00.522 --> 00:24:03.726
- I'm sorry, Dad. - It's okay.

00:24:03.726 --> 00:24:05.327
- I'm sorry. - Everything's fine.

00:24:08.230 --> 00:24:09.465
Let's go see Mom now. It's okay.

00:24:11.634 --> 00:24:12.668
How touching.

00:24:20.376 --> 00:24:21.577
Attention, everyone.

00:24:22.444 --> 00:24:24.013
The kids have been found.

00:24:24.780 --> 00:24:26.882
They're on their way back home now.

00:24:27.283 --> 00:24:28.917
Even if you see them, look the other way.

00:24:28.917 --> 00:24:30.486
Act like nothing happened.

00:24:30.486 --> 00:24:31.654
Please do so.

00:24:32.588 --> 00:24:34.290
Once again...

00:24:34.857 --> 00:24:39.395
Everyone in Yeonri-ri, you all did great work today.

00:24:42.731 --> 00:24:44.066
Seong Ji Gu.

00:24:44.066 --> 00:24:46.001
Do you know how worried I was?

00:24:46.568 --> 00:24:48.037
I'm sorry.

00:24:48.804 --> 00:24:50.239
Are you hurt?

00:24:51.874 --> 00:24:53.909
I missed you, Mom.

00:24:53.909 --> 00:24:55.778
I missed you too.

00:24:57.146 --> 00:24:58.280
My baby.

00:25:05.287 --> 00:25:06.121
Seong Ji Gu.

00:25:09.792 --> 00:25:10.893
Ji Sang.

00:25:13.128 --> 00:25:14.063
Ji Gu.

00:25:15.064 --> 00:25:16.665
Where were you?

00:25:17.933 --> 00:25:19.835
Do you know how much I looked for you?

00:25:23.405 --> 00:25:25.207
Are you okay, Ji Gu?

00:25:26.241 --> 00:25:28.377
It's okay. We're all here.

00:25:28.377 --> 00:25:30.913
We're all back together, safe and sound. Everything will be fine.

00:25:30.913 --> 00:25:32.815
It's okay.

00:25:35.384 --> 00:25:37.653
Let's go home now.

00:25:38.487 --> 00:25:40.789
Those parents went through hell today.

00:25:42.791 --> 00:25:44.360
You should go home too.

00:25:44.360 --> 00:25:45.294
Okay.

00:25:45.527 --> 00:25:47.796
Thank you for today.

00:25:48.564 --> 00:25:50.633
- Thank you so much. - Sure.

00:25:51.367 --> 00:25:53.702
Hey, boys. Don't ever do that again.

00:25:59.908 --> 00:26:01.043
Thank you.

00:26:01.043 --> 00:26:02.845
- Why are you out so late these days? - Thank you.

00:26:02.845 --> 00:26:04.113
Come home earlier.

00:26:04.113 --> 00:26:04.947
What a beautiful night.

00:26:16.358 --> 00:26:18.294
Do you feel better now?

00:26:19.161 --> 00:26:20.362
Because of you,

00:26:20.996 --> 00:26:22.298
our whole family,

00:26:22.598 --> 00:26:25.534
and the entire village were worried sick.

00:26:25.534 --> 00:26:27.236
Are you happy that your little brother cried his eyes out?

00:26:28.370 --> 00:26:30.239
Let's hear it then. What was the reason?

00:26:31.373 --> 00:26:32.875
Why were you...

00:26:32.875 --> 00:26:35.644
so desperate to go to Toronto?

00:26:38.347 --> 00:26:41.016
Carol has a new boyfriend.

00:26:41.016 --> 00:26:42.985
That darn Carol.

00:26:47.489 --> 00:26:49.024
You took your 9-year-old brother with you...

00:26:49.591 --> 00:26:52.261
just go see a girl? That's so dangerous.

00:26:52.261 --> 00:26:53.162
You too.

00:26:54.296 --> 00:26:56.231
You came to Seoul without asking too.

00:26:57.666 --> 00:26:59.268
Did you ask us for our opinions, Dad?

00:26:59.935 --> 00:27:02.171
You said 'let's go' so we came here, the middle of nowhere.

00:27:04.673 --> 00:27:06.775
So why can't I go? Why not?

00:27:06.775 --> 00:27:08.911
Don't you understand our situation? How can you say that?

00:27:09.545 --> 00:27:11.714
I'm going crazy here.

00:27:12.414 --> 00:27:14.216
You're giving me a headache.

00:27:14.216 --> 00:27:15.651
You're such a problem child.

00:27:16.118 --> 00:27:17.286
I'm going crazy here.

00:27:17.286 --> 00:27:18.420
You always dote on Seong Ji Cheon.

00:27:19.788 --> 00:27:21.256
Then there's Ji Gu, Ji Cheon's clone.

00:27:23.025 --> 00:27:24.426
You only need those two, right?

00:27:25.494 --> 00:27:26.462
I know it too.

00:27:28.597 --> 00:27:30.933
I'm just a problem child who can't even get into a university in Seoul.

00:27:32.501 --> 00:27:34.970
I'm not smart like Ji Cheon or Ji Gu.

00:27:37.740 --> 00:27:39.375
You think I'm hopeless, don't you?

00:27:40.409 --> 00:27:41.610
I never...

00:27:43.445 --> 00:27:44.213
I...

00:27:46.315 --> 00:27:49.084
You misunderstood.

00:27:49.084 --> 00:27:50.819
I'm doing everything for you.

00:27:50.819 --> 00:27:51.687
For me?

00:27:53.188 --> 00:27:54.123
No.

00:27:55.090 --> 00:27:57.259
You're just ashamed of me.

00:27:58.160 --> 00:27:59.328
What are you talking about?

00:28:00.095 --> 00:28:02.598
What kind of parent would be ashamed of their own child?

00:28:04.433 --> 00:28:05.334
Wait.

00:28:06.802 --> 00:28:08.904
Yes, you're right.

00:28:09.705 --> 00:28:11.640
You're always chasing after some girl.

00:28:12.041 --> 00:28:14.677
Not only did you get expelled because of her,

00:28:14.677 --> 00:28:16.278
but now you're trying to ruin your whole life too?

00:28:17.079 --> 00:28:18.414
Do you think...

00:28:18.414 --> 00:28:21.083
I enjoy fighting with you like this all the time?

00:28:21.083 --> 00:28:23.385
I'm doing this to help you become a decent person.

00:28:23.919 --> 00:28:24.853
Then what?

00:28:25.421 --> 00:28:27.089
If I'm not a decent person, what am I?

00:28:28.090 --> 00:28:30.859
Am I a dog? Should I crawl on all fours?

00:28:31.627 --> 00:28:32.394
Son.

00:28:32.962 --> 00:28:35.431
You're the son of Cho Mi Ryeo and Seong Tae Hun.

00:28:39.902 --> 00:28:41.036
I don't need that!

00:28:42.571 --> 00:28:43.472
That's...

00:28:44.840 --> 00:28:46.775
what I hate the most.

00:29:00.756 --> 00:29:01.590
It's okay.

00:29:03.058 --> 00:29:04.126
Calm down, honey.

00:29:05.127 --> 00:29:07.763
Ji Gu and Ji Sang's passports.

00:29:17.673 --> 00:29:20.609
Did your mother keep valuables like that?

00:29:21.310 --> 00:29:22.144
Yes.

00:29:23.212 --> 00:29:26.215
It's such an old-fashioned way, the kids would never think to look here.

00:29:35.891 --> 00:29:36.892
Ji Sang...

00:29:39.428 --> 00:29:40.796
It's because of me, isn't it?

00:29:43.198 --> 00:29:45.301
Do you think I treat him unfairly?

00:29:47.069 --> 00:29:49.405
All kids are different.

00:29:49.405 --> 00:29:50.973
How can you raise them all the same way?

00:29:55.277 --> 00:29:56.412
That's easy for you to say.

00:29:57.780 --> 00:29:58.747
You see...

00:29:59.615 --> 00:30:02.618
Dong Sik and Seon Ja ran away from home when they were young too.

00:30:02.618 --> 00:30:04.320
What happened today is nothing.

00:30:05.421 --> 00:30:06.221
You know what?

00:30:06.855 --> 00:30:08.924
I hate it when you blurt things out like that.

00:30:10.859 --> 00:30:12.761
I'm always the villain to the kids, aren't I?

00:30:13.362 --> 00:30:15.264
What have you been doing?

00:30:15.264 --> 00:30:17.633
If you hadn't been demoted, would we even be here right now?

00:30:18.534 --> 00:30:20.235
What have I been doing?

00:30:20.970 --> 00:30:21.937
I hung in there.

00:30:21.937 --> 00:30:24.540
To give the kids good education and feed them well.

00:30:24.740 --> 00:30:26.408
Do you think I enjoy living like this?

00:30:26.875 --> 00:30:30.312
You might've hung in there, but I fell apart every single day.

00:30:30.312 --> 00:30:31.714
In a foreign country where I didn't know anyone,

00:30:31.714 --> 00:30:33.248
with kids changing every day.

00:30:33.248 --> 00:30:35.651
Then you shouldn't have gone. Did I force you to go?

00:30:35.651 --> 00:30:37.152
You chose to do it.

00:30:48.397 --> 00:30:49.198
Sure.

00:30:50.165 --> 00:30:51.533
It's all my fault.

00:30:52.635 --> 00:30:53.502
Wait.

00:30:55.371 --> 00:30:58.073
I'm sorry, honey.

00:30:58.674 --> 00:31:01.110
I'm sorry. That's not what I meant. You know that.

00:31:01.110 --> 00:31:02.144
- Don't. - Come on.

00:31:13.222 --> 00:31:14.223
Darn.

00:31:25.501 --> 00:31:26.802
I thought you ran away again.

00:31:34.710 --> 00:31:36.245
I'm sorry you didn't make it to Canada.

00:31:38.314 --> 00:31:39.448
I'm going tomorrow.

00:31:43.819 --> 00:31:45.587
It must be nice getting to do whatever you want.

00:31:46.488 --> 00:31:47.756
Keep living like that.

00:31:49.825 --> 00:31:50.826
You're cursing me, aren't you?

00:31:51.927 --> 00:31:52.861
It's a curse.

00:31:53.128 --> 00:31:54.096
I'm serious.

00:31:58.834 --> 00:32:00.569
But leave the house after you're grown up.

00:32:02.438 --> 00:32:04.306
If you leave now, Mom and Dad will collapse.

00:32:44.480 --> 00:32:45.648
Honey?

00:32:46.982 --> 00:32:48.550
Cheon Sang Gu? What?

00:32:48.550 --> 00:32:50.419
'I completely screwed up in raising my kids.'

00:32:50.419 --> 00:32:51.954
Have you ever thought that way?

00:32:52.688 --> 00:32:54.356
I don't remember.

00:32:54.356 --> 00:32:56.392
And you still call yourself the head of this family?

00:32:57.159 --> 00:32:58.894
You deserve to be left alone in Korea.

00:32:59.328 --> 00:33:00.863
We're flying back to Canada.

00:33:04.566 --> 00:33:05.701
You fail as a father.

00:33:05.701 --> 00:33:06.669
No.

00:33:07.069 --> 00:33:08.671
I'll prove it with my cabbage.

00:33:10.105 --> 00:33:11.040
You fail.

00:33:11.040 --> 00:33:12.074
You fail.

00:33:12.074 --> 00:33:16.578
- You fail. - You fail.

00:33:16.578 --> 00:33:18.614
- You fail. - You fail.

00:33:18.614 --> 00:33:21.250
- You fail. - You fail.

00:33:26.355 --> 00:33:27.556
Cheon Sang Gu.

00:33:28.390 --> 00:33:29.258
Honey.

00:33:33.128 --> 00:33:34.496
Wake up, honey.

00:33:35.798 --> 00:33:38.667
Cabbage.

00:33:40.736 --> 00:33:41.570
Honey.

00:33:43.005 --> 00:33:44.640
You're not going to wake up?

00:33:44.873 --> 00:33:47.176
I don't want to be left alone in Korea.

00:33:47.810 --> 00:33:50.346
Honey, are you sick?

00:33:50.846 --> 00:33:53.082
Wake up. Let's go see a doctor.

00:33:53.682 --> 00:33:54.550
This isn't good.

00:33:55.050 --> 00:33:56.018
What did you say?

00:33:56.652 --> 00:33:57.753
I must...

00:33:58.921 --> 00:33:59.922
plow the field.

00:34:00.656 --> 00:34:02.191
Plow the field?

00:34:02.191 --> 00:34:03.759
I must plow the field.

00:34:04.593 --> 00:34:05.494
What?

00:34:07.496 --> 00:34:08.430
Hey.

00:34:08.731 --> 00:34:11.867
The guy from Mat Story... How come he's not here yet?

00:34:13.335 --> 00:34:14.970
Did you go to Andromeda last night?

00:34:14.970 --> 00:34:16.138
Didn't you hear the announcement?

00:34:16.572 --> 00:34:19.108
We knocked ourselves out with sleeping pills yesterday.

00:34:19.108 --> 00:34:20.576
How scary.

00:34:20.576 --> 00:34:22.077
Why? Can't you sleep well at night?

00:34:22.077 --> 00:34:24.813
Just a cup of makgeolli.

00:34:26.215 --> 00:34:28.150
How much did you drink?

00:34:29.852 --> 00:34:32.755
Last night, the Mat Story's kids ran away,

00:34:32.755 --> 00:34:33.656
and the whole village was in chaos.

00:34:33.656 --> 00:34:35.524
My goodness. Did you find them?

00:34:35.524 --> 00:34:36.792
Yes, of course.

00:34:36.792 --> 00:34:38.794
We blinked a few times and found them.

00:34:39.295 --> 00:34:40.296
They ran away?

00:34:41.430 --> 00:34:42.531
That's old-school.

00:34:42.531 --> 00:34:46.635
Even so, he shouldn't neglect the field.

00:34:47.670 --> 00:34:48.804
He must be sick.

00:34:49.672 --> 00:34:52.241
He must've collapsed from the shock.

00:34:52.441 --> 00:34:55.611
Kids and cabbage. You have to keep an eye on them for them to grow well.

00:34:55.978 --> 00:34:57.413
I'm sure he'll come after he checks on his kids.

00:34:57.413 --> 00:34:59.148
Leave him be. The field will be fine for a day or two.

00:35:01.550 --> 00:35:03.819
What? His wife is coming.

00:35:10.526 --> 00:35:12.528
I'm sure it's around here somewhere.

00:35:13.729 --> 00:35:16.165
All these roads look the same to me.

00:35:20.903 --> 00:35:22.171
Good morning.

00:35:23.706 --> 00:35:24.640
Good morning.

00:35:31.714 --> 00:35:33.115
What? I thought this was his office.

00:35:46.061 --> 00:35:47.129
What is all this?

00:35:48.297 --> 00:35:49.164
My goodness.

00:35:50.065 --> 00:35:51.634
When did he plant all these?

00:36:10.786 --> 00:36:13.856
Stop doing useless stuff and just rest.

00:36:20.229 --> 00:36:21.297
My goodness.

00:36:21.664 --> 00:36:24.800
He's about to go say hello to the Grim Reaper.

00:36:25.401 --> 00:36:26.769
He's too weak.

00:36:27.336 --> 00:36:29.638
Let's just leave it with him and go.

00:36:29.638 --> 00:36:31.507
- Go. - Okay. I'll be right back.

00:36:50.292 --> 00:36:52.027
Let's go. Let him rest.

00:36:54.229 --> 00:36:55.431
It's so hot.

00:37:12.314 --> 00:37:13.282
You poor thing.

00:37:15.618 --> 00:37:16.785
He's covered in sweat.

00:37:19.321 --> 00:37:20.222
What is it?

00:37:22.891 --> 00:37:24.093
I'm worried about Dad.

00:37:25.761 --> 00:37:27.696
Dad is sick. Go.

00:38:27.523 --> 00:38:28.791
I'm fine.

00:38:30.059 --> 00:38:30.993
I'm fine.

00:38:45.207 --> 00:38:48.377
Meet me at Dad's field after school today.

00:38:52.114 --> 00:38:53.749
So the rest of the field...

00:38:54.516 --> 00:38:56.285
I just make it look like this, right?

00:39:18.107 --> 00:39:19.108
I can do it.

00:39:20.709 --> 00:39:21.777
One, two, three.

00:39:23.946 --> 00:39:25.147
I'm doing it better than before.

00:39:31.020 --> 00:39:31.987
All this work...

00:39:33.355 --> 00:39:35.257
He's been doing it all by himself?

00:40:15.431 --> 00:40:16.298
Honey?

00:40:18.000 --> 00:40:18.867
Cho Mi Ryeo.

00:40:25.074 --> 00:40:25.941
Eat.

00:40:33.949 --> 00:40:36.251
Absolute rest until today.

00:40:48.330 --> 00:40:49.732
The house is a mess.

00:40:51.000 --> 00:40:53.435
Even if it's temporary, I should have taken better care of the house.

00:41:25.367 --> 00:41:26.635
How amazing.

00:41:33.709 --> 00:41:34.643
No.

00:41:35.177 --> 00:41:36.945
How are we supposed to do all this?

00:41:37.980 --> 00:41:39.181
You must use your feet.

00:41:39.181 --> 00:41:42.117
You're supposed to use your whole body to do this.

00:41:42.117 --> 00:41:44.053
You promised...

00:41:44.053 --> 00:41:45.654
to buy me a smartphone if I do this.

00:41:46.188 --> 00:41:47.389
We'll see.

00:41:47.389 --> 00:41:49.425
Why do you keep changing your words?

00:41:56.966 --> 00:41:59.601
You're good at digging.

00:42:02.137 --> 00:42:02.905
Me?

00:42:02.905 --> 00:42:05.140
You're good at this, Ji Sang.

00:42:06.542 --> 00:42:09.845
Ji Cheon. Come look at the row that Ji Sang dug.

00:42:12.381 --> 00:42:13.782
I just did it.

00:42:15.117 --> 00:42:17.486
You did it way better than I did.

00:42:19.955 --> 00:42:21.991
Tell Dad to stop doing research.

00:42:22.358 --> 00:42:24.760
This isn't research. It's just manual labor.

00:42:25.094 --> 00:42:26.295
Now you understand, right?

00:42:26.695 --> 00:42:29.498
Nothing in this world comes free. Not one thing is easy.

00:42:30.065 --> 00:42:30.766
Keep digging.

00:42:33.268 --> 00:42:34.336
Mom.

00:42:35.204 --> 00:42:36.071
Yes?

00:42:39.108 --> 00:42:40.643
- By the way, Mom... - Yes?

00:42:40.643 --> 00:42:42.911
What about Dad? Did he go see a doctor?

00:42:44.780 --> 00:42:46.982
No, he took his meds and is now resting.

00:42:47.316 --> 00:42:48.917
He'll go see a doctor tomorrow if he needs to.

00:42:49.785 --> 00:42:50.953
By the way, Mom...

00:42:51.987 --> 00:42:53.055
To tell you the truth...

00:42:53.589 --> 00:42:54.390
Yes?

00:42:55.557 --> 00:42:57.326
I'm a little scared of Dad.

00:42:59.295 --> 00:43:00.729
Why are you scared of him?

00:43:01.130 --> 00:43:03.565
You know how much he loves you.

00:43:03.565 --> 00:43:06.735
But he always looks at me...

00:43:07.102 --> 00:43:09.605
with those triangle eyes.

00:43:09.605 --> 00:43:11.940
He's not doing that on purpose.

00:43:12.975 --> 00:43:14.243
It feels awkward.

00:43:15.377 --> 00:43:16.578
I feel uncomfortable.

00:43:22.785 --> 00:43:23.953
Ask him to play with you.

00:43:25.554 --> 00:43:27.256
That's a great idea.

00:43:27.823 --> 00:43:29.391
And...

00:43:29.391 --> 00:43:30.592
Your dad...

00:43:30.926 --> 00:43:33.095
is actually really cute.

00:43:38.167 --> 00:43:39.234
That's not...

00:43:39.234 --> 00:43:40.269
He's cute.

00:43:43.138 --> 00:43:44.640
My goodness.

00:43:48.477 --> 00:43:50.779
It's true. Physical labor made my mind go blank.

00:43:50.779 --> 00:43:51.647
That's amazing.

00:43:53.148 --> 00:43:54.883
It was fun, wasn't it?

00:44:00.522 --> 00:44:02.324
We're not doing this again tomorrow, are we?

00:44:02.324 --> 00:44:04.059
We agreed to help Dad out.

00:44:04.059 --> 00:44:06.362
I can't do it.

00:44:08.831 --> 00:44:09.898
Chief.

00:44:11.600 --> 00:44:12.935
Hello.

00:44:12.935 --> 00:44:14.603
Hi.

00:44:15.771 --> 00:44:18.841
Chief. Do you farm at home too?

00:44:19.708 --> 00:44:20.542
What?

00:44:21.243 --> 00:44:22.544
Come here, Ji Gu.

00:44:22.544 --> 00:44:23.579
This.

00:44:24.446 --> 00:44:26.849
Don't worry. I'll walk him home later.

00:44:27.116 --> 00:44:28.550
Goodbye. Don't worry about him.

00:44:34.156 --> 00:44:36.191
The cow dung smell is legendary.

00:44:36.959 --> 00:44:37.926
I'll shower first.

00:44:37.926 --> 00:44:39.461
No, you can't.

00:44:39.461 --> 00:44:41.797
I seriously feel like I'm going to throw up. I'll go first.

00:44:44.133 --> 00:44:45.034
What?

00:44:47.503 --> 00:44:48.404
What's this?

00:44:49.405 --> 00:44:50.906
Did you work in the field?

00:44:51.407 --> 00:44:53.342
What did you do instead of resting?

00:44:54.109 --> 00:44:56.278
Did you clean all this?

00:44:56.879 --> 00:44:59.982
I felt a bit better, so I cleaned up a little.

00:45:00.716 --> 00:45:01.850
I also made curry.

00:45:02.384 --> 00:45:04.086
- Let's go. - Let's go.

00:45:05.554 --> 00:45:06.422
Go wash up.

00:45:07.122 --> 00:45:10.459
Everything here is for us to eat.

00:45:11.093 --> 00:45:12.995
The things that grow in the field are for us to sell.

00:45:14.029 --> 00:45:16.265
I read somewhere that...

00:45:16.265 --> 00:45:18.567
the more microorganisms there are in the soil,

00:45:18.567 --> 00:45:21.170
the better the crops grow.

00:45:21.170 --> 00:45:23.706
Do you take care of microorganisms, too?

00:45:24.840 --> 00:45:25.708
Microorganisms?

00:45:27.009 --> 00:45:28.711
Microorganisms.

00:45:28.711 --> 00:45:31.146
Right. We use compost. Fertilizer.

00:45:31.747 --> 00:45:33.115
Then...

00:45:33.482 --> 00:45:35.784
I heard that if you use compost tea,

00:45:35.784 --> 00:45:39.154
it reduces root stress. Is that true?

00:45:39.922 --> 00:45:43.225
I've never tried that before.

00:45:43.225 --> 00:45:44.293
I'll try it and let you know.

00:45:44.293 --> 00:45:46.962
You sure are curious, Seong Ji Gu.

00:45:46.962 --> 00:45:48.263
Are you going to be a farmer when you grow up?

00:45:49.298 --> 00:45:53.335
Your field is full of cabbage,

00:45:53.335 --> 00:45:55.504
but cabbage doesn't grow well in my dad's field.

00:45:56.271 --> 00:45:59.074
Did you go to the field today?

00:45:59.475 --> 00:46:03.112
Yes, I was just talking while everyone else was digging.

00:46:03.379 --> 00:46:05.681
They said I will be digging plenty once I grow up.

00:46:09.251 --> 00:46:12.521
Crops grow

00:46:12.521 --> 00:46:13.622
when they hear people's footsteps.

00:46:14.390 --> 00:46:16.058
If they hear people coming, they can't help but grow.

00:46:16.992 --> 00:46:20.029
Can you go there with me again later?

00:46:20.929 --> 00:46:21.864
Why?

00:46:21.864 --> 00:46:23.866
I saw earlier that...

00:46:23.866 --> 00:46:25.701
some of them looked weak.

00:46:26.635 --> 00:46:28.504
I want them to hear our footsteps.

00:46:31.340 --> 00:46:34.576
If you don't sleep at night, you won't grow either.

00:46:35.044 --> 00:46:36.278
That's not good.

00:46:36.945 --> 00:46:39.415
If neither I nor the cabbage grows,

00:46:39.415 --> 00:46:40.883
Dad will be sad.

00:46:48.657 --> 00:46:49.725
Good work today.

00:46:50.592 --> 00:46:52.394
Let's eat.

00:46:52.394 --> 00:46:53.262
Okay.

00:47:01.103 --> 00:47:03.706
Dad, this is really good.

00:47:03.706 --> 00:47:04.707
Really?

00:47:05.074 --> 00:47:06.642
Thanks, Ji Gu.

00:47:06.642 --> 00:47:08.944
But it's just because you're hungry...

00:47:08.944 --> 00:47:10.646
from all that labor.

00:47:11.614 --> 00:47:14.483
Did you eat curry every day?

00:47:16.452 --> 00:47:17.820
It goes well with kimchi.

00:47:18.420 --> 00:47:19.989
I ate rice with seaweed.

00:47:20.255 --> 00:47:22.591
When I got tired of that, I ate rice with curry.

00:47:32.468 --> 00:47:33.769
My goodness.

00:47:36.071 --> 00:47:37.373
Look at the field.

00:47:38.841 --> 00:47:42.511
Did they plow the field or break it?

00:47:44.313 --> 00:47:45.314
My goodness.

00:47:51.186 --> 00:47:52.087
What's that?

00:47:56.825 --> 00:47:58.093
Goodness.

00:47:59.428 --> 00:48:02.464
His family worked hard,

00:48:03.032 --> 00:48:05.534
but all the seedlings will die if they're left like this.

00:48:07.936 --> 00:48:09.838
Goodness.

00:48:11.740 --> 00:48:13.976
I just came out here to exercise, okay?

00:48:13.976 --> 00:48:16.078
I didn't come out here to help you, Seong Tae Hun.

00:48:20.683 --> 00:48:23.986
A field comes back to life along with people's footsteps.

00:48:24.787 --> 00:48:27.890
I felt bad seeing your wife and kids working hard in the field,

00:48:31.160 --> 00:48:32.695
so I came out to exercise.

00:48:34.897 --> 00:48:37.933
I came to work my biceps, forearms, and do some squats.

00:48:55.184 --> 00:48:56.251
Unbelievable.

00:48:57.119 --> 00:49:00.122
You and the kids were farming geniuses?

00:49:02.024 --> 00:49:03.492
We did a good job, didn't we?

00:49:06.428 --> 00:49:08.097
Seeing how hard you and the kids worked,

00:49:08.097 --> 00:49:09.632
I think I'm all better now.

00:49:12.434 --> 00:49:15.704
Ji Sang worked on that side of the field.

00:49:15.704 --> 00:49:17.539
I was surprised to see how good he was.

00:49:17.539 --> 00:49:18.440
Really?

00:49:24.280 --> 00:49:25.047
Honey.

00:49:25.614 --> 00:49:28.784
Let's not worry too much about Ji Sang now, okay?

00:49:29.418 --> 00:49:30.486
Let's take it slow...

00:49:30.953 --> 00:49:35.157
and help him find what he's good at, what he wants to do, okay?

00:49:36.191 --> 00:49:38.560
Even so, I'm sending him to college.

00:49:41.196 --> 00:49:43.565
Of course. He should go to college.

00:49:44.433 --> 00:49:46.135
Let's go inside.

00:49:51.240 --> 00:49:52.141
Honey.

00:49:52.508 --> 00:49:55.077
I think they grew because we watered them yesterday.

00:49:55.077 --> 00:49:56.378
It's amazing.

00:49:56.378 --> 00:49:57.579
Of course.

00:49:57.880 --> 00:49:59.581
They don't grow on their own either.

00:49:59.581 --> 00:50:02.217
They only grow as much as we care for them.

00:50:03.919 --> 00:50:05.054
Honey.

00:50:06.355 --> 00:50:08.924
Let's go visit the kids' school.

00:50:10.326 --> 00:50:11.160
Their school?

00:50:12.661 --> 00:50:15.698
In your right hand, hold the pointed stick.

00:50:15.698 --> 00:50:17.900
In your left hand, hold the round stick.

00:50:18.233 --> 00:50:19.835
Deongdeok.

00:50:19.835 --> 00:50:21.870
Kungdeok kung. I'll demonstrate.

00:50:25.341 --> 00:50:27.009
Deongdeok kungdeok kung.

00:50:27.009 --> 00:50:28.444
Good. Deongdeok.

00:50:30.112 --> 00:50:35.084
Deongdeok kungdeok kung.

00:50:36.185 --> 00:50:38.187
He loves to read.

00:50:39.021 --> 00:50:39.855
Ji Gu.

00:50:41.090 --> 00:50:41.957
Seong Ji Gu.

00:50:42.858 --> 00:50:43.892
Son.

00:50:49.164 --> 00:50:52.935
(Cafeteria)

00:51:04.146 --> 00:51:05.180
Hello.

00:51:06.448 --> 00:51:07.416
Hello.

00:51:07.416 --> 00:51:10.319
Bo Mi. Thank you so much for the other day.

00:51:10.319 --> 00:51:11.687
No, no.

00:51:11.687 --> 00:51:13.389
We didn't get to thank you properly that day.

00:51:13.389 --> 00:51:14.523
You went through an ordeal, didn't you?

00:51:14.523 --> 00:51:16.058
Not at all. I didn't.

00:51:16.058 --> 00:51:18.427
Thank you so much for everything you did.

00:51:18.427 --> 00:51:19.928
There's no need. You must've been quite worried.

00:51:19.928 --> 00:51:21.630
They left without a word.

00:51:21.630 --> 00:51:24.099
I was so shocked that I thought my heart was going to drop.

00:51:24.099 --> 00:51:25.701
It's such a relief they were found.

00:51:25.701 --> 00:51:28.237
We are so grateful.

00:51:28.237 --> 00:51:30.205
I was so worried that I was terrified...

00:51:39.348 --> 00:51:40.382
Bo Mi.

00:51:42.451 --> 00:51:44.586
Are you getting ready to run away too?

00:51:44.586 --> 00:51:45.454
What?

00:51:45.854 --> 00:51:47.856
Why are you keeping secrets from your family?

00:51:48.991 --> 00:51:50.025
You see...

00:51:50.025 --> 00:51:53.128
If those secrets pile up one by one, they'll become really heavy.

00:51:53.128 --> 00:51:54.163
Do you want me to help a little?

00:51:55.397 --> 00:51:57.533
- Mat Story... - No, Bo Mi. Please.

00:51:59.802 --> 00:52:00.669
Why?

00:52:00.669 --> 00:52:03.072
What's wrong with a med student working part-time in a cafeteria?

00:52:04.373 --> 00:52:07.743
Things that are nothing if you talk about them right away...

00:52:07.743 --> 00:52:09.611
keep growing inside if you bottle them up.

00:52:09.611 --> 00:52:11.380
When they finally explode, it'll hurt even more.

00:52:17.353 --> 00:52:20.956
Why did your brothers run away?

00:52:21.523 --> 00:52:26.228
I guess Ji Sang's girlfriend started dating another guy.

00:52:27.296 --> 00:52:29.031
So he said he had to go to Toronto.

00:52:30.099 --> 00:52:30.866
It's ridiculous, isn't it?

00:52:31.166 --> 00:52:33.569
No. I think it's cool.

00:52:34.203 --> 00:52:36.538
That little kid sure learned about love.

00:52:36.939 --> 00:52:39.375
What can he do about someone who doesn't feel the same way anymore?

00:52:39.875 --> 00:52:41.210
Well...

00:52:42.077 --> 00:52:43.812
Isn't what I feel the most important?

00:52:44.380 --> 00:52:46.181
What I want to do,

00:52:46.181 --> 00:52:47.483
how I want to do it...

00:52:47.983 --> 00:52:49.652
Only I know that, right?

00:52:56.992 --> 00:52:58.494
- Honey. - Yes?

00:52:59.261 --> 00:52:59.995
You see...

00:53:01.130 --> 00:53:02.097
Well...

00:53:03.365 --> 00:53:04.333
You see...

00:53:06.368 --> 00:53:08.203
Never mind. Let's go.

00:53:10.906 --> 00:53:13.642
It's nice coming to the kids' school with you.

00:53:23.953 --> 00:53:25.254
To be honest,

00:53:26.956 --> 00:53:28.257
I have a condition.

00:53:29.091 --> 00:53:29.959
What?

00:53:30.793 --> 00:53:32.294
Are you sick?

00:53:34.330 --> 00:53:35.364
A butting-in condition.

00:53:38.067 --> 00:53:39.935
I couldn't help but notice it.

00:53:39.935 --> 00:53:42.404
When someone sits there all day with such lonely eyes,

00:53:42.404 --> 00:53:44.039
my condition starts acting up.

00:53:45.407 --> 00:53:48.877
I don't have anywhere to go, and I don't want to go home.

00:53:52.014 --> 00:53:53.182
I know a great place.

00:53:55.084 --> 00:53:56.352
Do you want to go pick apples?

00:53:56.652 --> 00:53:57.720
Apples?

00:54:14.203 --> 00:54:15.170
Do you like apples?

00:54:16.772 --> 00:54:17.640
I don't know.

00:54:20.009 --> 00:54:21.477
Try one. It's sweet.

00:54:30.252 --> 00:54:31.020
It's good.

00:54:32.421 --> 00:54:34.690
These are Gamong apples. They are amazing.

00:54:34.690 --> 00:54:36.992
Sometimes I come here to help out,

00:54:36.992 --> 00:54:39.495
and when they're in season, I give them to the kids as snacks.

00:54:39.495 --> 00:54:40.429
So I know about these apples well.

00:54:41.096 --> 00:54:44.099
Was it always your dream to be a nutritionist?

00:54:45.768 --> 00:54:47.336
I always wanted to cook.

00:54:47.870 --> 00:54:50.472
But while I was preparing to become a chef, before I knew it,

00:54:51.307 --> 00:54:52.274
I ended up working at this school.

00:54:54.243 --> 00:54:56.312
Do you like what you do?

00:54:57.546 --> 00:54:58.914
Of course.

00:54:59.214 --> 00:55:01.917
I really love this job.

00:55:03.953 --> 00:55:05.754
When I see kids grow up eating the food I make,

00:55:06.789 --> 00:55:08.123
I feel really proud.

00:55:10.592 --> 00:55:12.661
I don't know what I like.

00:55:14.396 --> 00:55:17.032
Is that really a problem? That's actually a good thing.

00:55:18.100 --> 00:55:19.134
What's good about it?

00:55:20.269 --> 00:55:21.570
You can start figuring it out now.

00:55:22.371 --> 00:55:24.873
There's fun in searching, you know.

00:55:28.944 --> 00:55:31.480
You look happy.

00:55:32.381 --> 00:55:33.215
I like that.

00:55:37.886 --> 00:55:38.988
What I mean is...

00:55:39.855 --> 00:55:40.689
You see...

00:55:44.093 --> 00:55:44.960
I...

00:55:46.795 --> 00:55:47.763
have something to tell you.

00:56:21.797 --> 00:56:22.831
Get home safe.

00:56:28.971 --> 00:56:31.173
What we did today...

00:56:34.376 --> 00:56:35.344
A secret.

00:56:35.744 --> 00:56:36.745
Let's keep it a secret.

00:56:37.379 --> 00:56:38.480
Thanks for hanging out with me today.

00:56:39.481 --> 00:56:40.349
Here.

00:56:43.786 --> 00:56:47.356
I heard the scooter. Why isn't she coming in?

00:56:47.356 --> 00:56:48.123
I don't know.

00:56:51.360 --> 00:56:53.362
Bo Mi, are you home?

00:56:55.030 --> 00:56:55.731
What?

00:56:57.032 --> 00:56:57.766
Hey.

00:57:00.703 --> 00:57:01.637
I should go now.

00:57:02.938 --> 00:57:03.839
Wait.

00:57:04.406 --> 00:57:05.374
I...

00:57:13.549 --> 00:57:17.186
Can we go to the apple orchard again sometime?

00:57:25.260 --> 00:57:26.128
I'm off now.

00:57:32.801 --> 00:57:33.969
Yes, I'm home.

00:57:36.405 --> 00:57:38.540
You're home.

00:57:38.540 --> 00:57:40.676
- Bo Mi is home. - Bo Mi is home.

00:57:41.343 --> 00:57:43.412
My treasure.

00:57:43.412 --> 00:57:45.514
Your mom and I were doing this. One, two.

00:57:45.514 --> 00:57:47.783
- Did you wait long? - That's enough.

00:57:49.618 --> 00:57:50.919
Come here.

00:58:12.541 --> 00:58:13.575
I'm so proud of you.

00:58:14.610 --> 00:58:17.212
I roll around in the manure field for you.

00:58:18.013 --> 00:58:19.515
Wow. This is...

00:58:20.549 --> 00:58:21.650
What does it say?

00:58:34.763 --> 00:58:35.798
What's this?

00:58:48.978 --> 00:58:49.812
Dad?

00:58:52.081 --> 00:58:52.982
Seong Ji Cheon.

00:58:54.249 --> 00:58:55.851
What are you up to these days?

00:58:57.152 --> 00:58:58.020
What?

00:58:59.421 --> 00:59:02.224
You should be back in med school, so what were you doing there?

00:59:03.626 --> 00:59:05.661
You saw me earlier?

00:59:06.228 --> 00:59:07.963
You see...

00:59:09.031 --> 00:59:11.800
I thought I would make some pocket money by working part-time...

00:59:11.800 --> 00:59:13.202
Why are you lying to me?

00:59:13.969 --> 00:59:15.204
Then what is this?

00:59:23.812 --> 00:59:26.181
(Withdrawal Form, reason, personal)

00:59:29.785 --> 00:59:32.354
I already submitted the withdrawal form.

00:59:32.955 --> 00:59:34.356
It'll be official after a face-to-face talk.

00:59:34.356 --> 00:59:35.224
What?

00:59:36.892 --> 00:59:37.726
What?

00:59:38.694 --> 00:59:39.862
Forget it.

00:59:39.862 --> 00:59:41.997
Go back to med school tomorrow.

00:59:41.997 --> 00:59:42.898
Go and beg them.

00:59:44.133 --> 00:59:45.534
I can't go back.

00:59:45.534 --> 00:59:47.636
Why not?

00:59:47.636 --> 00:59:49.471
Don't you start causing trouble too, okay?

00:59:49.938 --> 00:59:51.540
Go back to med school tomorrow.

00:59:51.540 --> 00:59:53.108
I won't tell Mom.

00:59:53.108 --> 00:59:55.811
Go take back the withdrawal form.

00:59:58.447 --> 00:59:59.381
To tell you the truth...

01:00:07.056 --> 01:00:07.923
I...

01:00:09.625 --> 01:00:10.626
killed a man.

01:00:13.996 --> 01:00:14.863
What?

01:00:18.367 --> 01:00:20.836
Seong Ji Cheon. Put the scalpel down.

01:00:20.836 --> 01:00:21.870
The patient's blood pressure is dropping.

01:00:21.870 --> 01:00:22.738
Right now.

01:00:24.006 --> 01:00:25.207
We need to start CPR. Now.

01:00:25.207 --> 01:00:26.775
You punk. Can you not hear me?

01:00:27.609 --> 01:00:30.412
Can you not hear me? Put down the scalpel!

01:00:30.412 --> 01:00:31.246
Put down the scalpel.

01:00:42.758 --> 01:00:43.993
Unexpected variables...

01:00:44.426 --> 01:00:46.862
always explode from the quietest one.

01:01:12.955 --> 01:01:15.891
(Cabbage Your Life)

01:01:15.891 --> 01:01:18.394
I ran away because I wanted to hide.

01:01:18.927 --> 01:01:21.430
Does it bother you that I'm going to Seoul?

01:01:21.430 --> 01:01:23.032
If Ji Cheon causes a problem too, I really can't go on.

01:01:23.032 --> 01:01:24.700
No, that's not what I meant.

01:01:24.700 --> 01:01:26.368
Whatever I do, however I live,

01:01:26.368 --> 01:01:27.236
I'll be the one to decide.

01:01:27.603 --> 01:01:30.306
What exactly did you do for this family?

01:01:30.639 --> 01:01:32.074
From now on,

01:01:32.074 --> 01:01:33.742
I'm going to start learning about my sons.

01:01:33.742 --> 01:01:35.277
Why are you suddenly acting like we're close?

01:01:35.277 --> 01:01:36.612
Just keep doing what you always did.

01:01:36.612 --> 01:01:38.948
What am I supposed to do?

01:01:38.948 --> 01:01:41.650
You grew those cabbages with your sweat and tears.

01:01:41.650 --> 01:01:43.652
You want to hand them over to those people again?

01:01:44.320 --> 01:01:45.788
When you said you were going to farm here,

01:01:45.788 --> 01:01:47.156
why do you think I was against it?

01:01:48.724 --> 01:01:50.726
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)

